area: imperative summary, 72 characters at most

# Problem: what was wrong or missing, and who sees it.
#
# Change: what this commit does and why this approach. Name the fix
# when the commit also refactors.
#
# Verified: the commands run and what they printed; what was not run.
#
# Area: the noun of what changes (install, http, css, docs, ci).
# "type(scope): summary" is also accepted.
#
# Trailers (last, after a blank line):
#   Fixes #123
#   Fixes: <12 hex> ("subject of the culprit commit")
#   BREAKING CHANGE: what to do instead
#
# No assistant or bot attribution. Signed-off-by only when the README asks.
# Lines starting with "#" are dropped. Rules: docs/standards/commit-format.md
